      "query": "How does inflation affect bond prices?",
      "cached_at": "2026-11-22T22:09:11+00:00",
      "response": {
        "answer": "Inflation can decrease the value of bond prices. When inflation rises, the real value of the fixed interest payments and principal repayment on a bond decreases [1]. This makes existing bonds less attractive to investors, who may demand a higher yield to compensate for the reduced purchasing power. As a result, bond prices typically fall when inflation increases [1].",
